Zero boot/container growth to 384 KiB kernel slots
2026-11-15 UTC

Scope and provenance
Audited every line of bios.zero, loader.zero, loader32.zero, image.zero,
iso.zero and build.sh. The OS loaders and container writers are original
Zero source, compiled by build/selfhost-core-fs-stage2. No assembler or
linker was used. Bash/file tools prepare slots and run tests; QEMU, SeaBIOS,
OVMF, xorriso, fsck.fat and mtools are external validation dependencies.
The compiler agent independently tested the new INT15/E820 ABI primitive;
its evidence is verification/compiler-fs/values/real-vm.

Final source, BIOS binary and two private ISO hashes are in
final-inputs.sha256. The standalone full-slot ISO is also identified by
tail-iso.sha256. Tests never used build/data.img or build/data.vdi writable.

Final binary sizes
BIOS: 13865 bytes, maximum16384.
AMD64 EFI: 14336 bytes, maximum65536.
IA32 EFI: 20992 bytes, maximum65536.
FAT16: 16777216 bytes.
ISO: 8616 * 2048 = 17645568 bytes.

Implementation and full source audit
Both kernel slots are393216 bytes, and all loader/builder/build limits agree.
BIOS reads12 separate32KiB requests, ending at physical80000 exclusively.
The optical extents are BIOS32..39, kernel64 40..231, kernel32 232..423 and
EFI FAT424..8615. Each UEFI loader allocates96 code pages and accepts file
sizes1..393216. IA32's maximum code base isfff9f000 for its below4GiB guard.
Both EFI GetInfo paths now validate returned size80..512 before FileSize.

The BIOS validates conventional-memory and EBDA boundaries before payload
reads. Its high stack pool is100000..3fffff, with entry stack top400000.
Complete bounded E820 enumeration must prove this whole pool is usable RAM;
enabled reserved overlap, missing coverage, invalid/oversized map, or relevant
64-bit range overflow stops boot. Adjacent or unordered usable intervals are
merged. At most256 intervals fit4000..47ff and are discarded before that
space becomes a page directory. E8206600, VBE6200/6400, locals6f00 and BIOS
code7c00..bbff remain separate. The real-mode local count fits its256-byte
bank. The compiled BIOS fits before the fourth page directory atc000.
VBE now rejects a framebuffer below4MiB so graphics cannot alias the new pool.
The existing first4GiB identity map and text fallback are retained.

Both EFI paths retain short-read accumulation, zero-progress refusal, exact
status checks, separate completion flags and dedicated allocated stacks.
GOP validation is completed before the final memory map; after the first exit
attempt only GetMemoryMap/ExitBootServices call firmware, with four attempts.
The map is bounded to64KiB. Returned IA32 UINTN values use cleared high halves.

FAT kernel chains are260..1027 and1028..1795,768 clusters each; EFI chains are
unchanged. Both FATs derive from the same rules. All four file sizes/extents,
input EOF boundaries and ISO paired-endian fields were checked. PE reads are
within the first sector; all validated raw section ends fit the64KiB slot.
Streaming readers/writers retain partial-I/O handling and EINTR retry.
build.sh rejects oversized binaries before padding, checks final image sizes,
and replaces only named generated artifacts; it never creates or formats
persistent data disks. bash -n passed for the build and both new test scripts.

Four complete-slot runtime probes: PASS
Source: review-tests/boot-growth/slot-tail.zero.
Orchestration: review-tests/boot-growth/run-tail.sh.
Each architecture's unique string offset is discovered in its compiled raw
binary, substituted into the source and verified unchanged after recompiling.
The runtime checks markers at byte offsets131071,131072,262143,262144,393215.
Thus reaching the entry instruction alone cannot pass this test. It also
checks handoff code-pages96, stack-pool size/base, the full64KiB reserve range,
and writes/reads both arena ends and the pool's lower end.

BIOS32: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,-lm,-pae,128MiB, SeaBIOS.
BIOS64: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,128MiB, SeaBIOS.
UEFI32: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,-lm,128MiB, IA32 OVMF4M.
UEFI64: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,128MiB, AMD64 OVMF4M.
Every final serial log contains BOOT384 TAIL/ARENA/POOL PASS and every QEMU
debug-exit status is1, the expected successful exit encoding.
Evidence: bios32-tail.*, bios64-tail.*, uefi32-tail.*, uefi64-tail.*.
Private OVMF variable stores were used. These four probe VMs all exited.

Before the final audit hardening, the enlarged containers also booted frozen
0.6 kernels to the complete ZeroFS/terminal prompt on all four paths. The
saved bios32.serial, bios64.serial, uefi32.serial and uefi64.serial show this
compatibility smoke. They are not final integrated0.7 kernel evidence.

Low-memory refusal: PASS
The final BIOS with QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,-lm,-pae and3MiB guest RAM prints
ZERO BIOS: stack pool overlaps reserved memory
before any entering-kernel message. The halted VM was stopped by a12-second
test timeout. Evidence: bios-lowram.serial, .qemu and .status.

Container inspection and failure cases: PASS
Orchestration: review-tests/boot-growth/check-containers.sh.
fsck.fat reports7 files,1794/32479 clusters with no error. xorriso recognizes
8616 sectors and BIOSLBA32/load32 plus EFILBA424/load32768. Four ISO-extracted
payloads exactly match inputs; four FAT-extracted payloads also exactly match.
The FAT copies match each other. Final inputs have exact917504-byte FAT and
17580032-byte ISO input lengths. Each writer passes all six outcomes:
exact input0, one-byte short2, one-byte excess3, malformed header2,
unreadable input1, /dev/full output4. See container-results.txt and format logs.

Data preservation and limits
data.img SHA256 c730241fb30f5516867c751006951a2878f360319195ee975411a05f040f27e8
data.vdi SHA256 7f58fb36c934405757da797ca65f2dddef3858e69107f43e2cae59d14c89bc5f
Both match their pre-task hashes. There are no live test QEMU processes.
The native VirtualBox executable and physical hardware were not tested.
The BIOS layout remains a fixed PC optical-boot contract, not an MBR/USB
installer or a general RAM allocator. These probes establish boot/container
capacity and ownership; filesystem-driver correctness and the final combined
kernel are separate integration work owned by the parent task.
